+ Offset pagination uses OFFSET and LIMIT/pageSize. The database still needs to scan and skip records before the offset.
    Easy to implement
    Supported natively by Spring Data JPA and JPA
    Supports page numbers (page 1, 2, 3...)
    Poor performance and scalability for large datasets
+ Keyset pagination uses the last record (cursor) to continue fetching data.
    Better performance and scalability because the database can use indexes directly
    More consistent for real-time data
    Not natively supported by JPA
    Does not support direct page numbers easily